    "scope": "Scoped Windows Store/ledger/federation/maintenance/digest checks. No whole-native/platform acceptance. Any setup failures remain recorded; no fixture is gated away."
  },
  "findings": [
    "Original real SQLite regressions fail before correction: lock cancellation waits 2.2579239s after its signal; expired serialization is followed by 632.1099ms of additional lock waiting. A separate uncontended record publication cancels during serialization yet is admitted before correction.",
    "Connection-owned SQLite client data now holds the policy. Callback lookup uses the owning connection, not a Store address; removal/closure fails closed. No global/thread-local callback dispatch, SQL from callbacks, dependency upgrade or automatic transaction retry.",
    "Checked Store lock waits consult actual monotonic time and the original host cancellation flags before and after each requested <=2ms sleep. Ledger admission keeps that policy. Generic record/create/replace/delete check again after serialization.",
    "Nine integration tests cover real locked cancellation, serialization exhaustion, three uncontended cancelled record mutations, ledger accounting recovery, brief lock success with exact Unicode data and moving a connection out of a dropped Store to another thread. A library test removes and reinstalls the registration.",
    "All 17 selected native result groups execute with no-fail-fast. The only two failures are unchanged real symlink fixture creation OS1314 in federation and maintenance; no security test is bypassed.",
    "Original red/initial-green logs are development traces. The final unchanged-source manifest is the authoritative final validation input set. Constructor schema setup, other raw SQLite connections, hosted platform acceptance and broader STATUS/R1-R9 remain separate gates."
  ],
  "references": [
    "https://sqlite.org/c3ref/busy_handler.html",
    "https://sqlite.org/c3ref/get_clientdata.html"
  ],
